<a href="#B73" rel="footnote" style="display:none"></a><p>Zerhouni, O., Rougier, M., &amp; Muller, D. (2016). “Who (really) is Charlie?” French cities with lower implicit prejudice toward Arabs demonstrated larger participation rates in Charlie Hebdo rallies. <em>International Review of Social Psychology</em>, 29(1), 69–76. DOI: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://doi.org/10.5334/irsp.50">https://doi.org/10.5334/irsp.50</a><a href="#main-text-B73" class="scroll-link" data-scroll="#main-text-B73" aria-label="Jump to citation B73">   <svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" class="fvKGdu bgJTSC kIIaya gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya" width="1em" height="1em"><use href="/api/2.27.0/spritesheet#arrow-outward"></use></svg></a></p>
