}]\ncc:[\"$\",\"li\",\"137\",{\"id\":\"B69\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B69\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"U.S. Census Bureau. (2009). DP02 Selected social characteristics in the United States. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"American FactFinder\"}],\". Retrieved from: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"http://factfinder2.census.gov/\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"http://factfinder2.census.gov/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B69\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B69\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B69\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\ncd:[\"$\",\"li\",\"139\",{\"id\":\"B70\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B70\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"U.S. Census Bureau. (2010). DP-1 profile of general population and housing characteristics: 2010. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"American FactFinder\"}],\".\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B70\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B70\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B70\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\nce:[\"$\",\"li\",\"141\",{\"id\":\"B71\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B71\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Van Honk, J., Tuiten, A., Van Den Hout, M., Putman, P., De Haan, E., \u0026 Stam, H. (2001). Selective attention to unmasked and masked threatening words: Relationships to trait anger and anxiety. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"Personality and Individual Differences\"}],\", 30(4), 711–720. DOI: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0191-8869(00)00160-4\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0191-8869(00)00160-4\"}],[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B71\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B71\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B71\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\ncf:[\"$\",\"li\",\"143\",{\"id\":\"B72\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B72\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Wilkowski, B. M., \u0026 Robinson, M. D. (2010). The anatomy of anger: An integrative cognitive model of trait anger and reactive aggression. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"Journal of Personality\"}],\", 78(1), 9–38. DOI: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-6494.2009.00607.x\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-6494.2009.00607.x\"}],[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B72\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B72\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B72\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\nd0:[\"$\",\"li\",\"145\",{\"id\":\"B73\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B73\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Zerhouni, O., Rougier, M., \u0026 Muller, D. (2016). “Who (really) is Charlie?” French cities with lower implicit prejudice toward Arabs demonstrated larger participation rates in Charlie Hebdo rallies. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"International Review of Social Psychology\"}],\", 29(1), 69–76. DOI: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.5334/irsp.50\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"https://doi.org/10.5334/irsp.50\"}],[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B73\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B73\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B73\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\nd1:[\"$\",\"li\",\"147\",{\"id\":\"B74\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"#B74\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"Zou, H., \u0026 Hastie, T. (2005). Regularization and variable selection via the Elastic Net. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"Journal of the Royal Statistical Society, Series B (Statistical Methodology)\"}],\", 67(2), 301–320. DOI: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"3\",{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2005.00503.x\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2005.00503.x\"}],[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"scroll-link\",\"href\":\"#main-text-B74\",\"data-scroll\":\"#main-text-B74\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to citation B74\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"   \",[\"$\",\"$L25\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"arrow-outward\",\"className\":\"gljXA gloUs nVRGN kIIaya\"}]]}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\nb:null\n10:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Tweeted Anger Predicts County-Level Results of the 2016 United States Presidential Election | International Review of Social Psychology\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"DC.Creator\",\"content\":\"Bernecker, Katharina\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"DC.Creator\",\"content\":\"Wenzler, Michael\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"DC.Creator\",\"content\":\"Sassenberg, Kai\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"DC.Description.abstract\",\"content\":\"In the aftermath of the 2016 United States presidential election, experts and journalists speculated that angry voters had supported the unexpected winner Donald Trump. The present study used a sample of 148 million tweets posted by U.S. citizens from across 1,347 counties, classified with regard to emotional content, to predict the election results at county level. As expected, Donald Trump received more support in counties where people tweeted more anger and negative emotions, even when various county characteristics and conservative vote choice in the preceding presidential election were controlled. These findings might be an outcome of emotional resonance—voters being attracted by political appeals that match their emotions—because Trump used more anger and negative emotion words in his campaign than the other presidential candidates in 2012 and 2016. The findings suggest that negative emotions played a critical role in the 2016 presidential election.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"DC.date\",\"content\":\"2019-05-03T11:21:22+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.available\",\"content\":\"2019-05-03T11:21:22+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.created\",\"content\":\"2019-05-03T11:21:22+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.dateAccepted\",\"content\":\"2019-03-29T08:52:04+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.dateCopyrighted\",\"content\":\"2019\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.dateSubmitted\",\"content\":\"2019-01-28T13:18:00+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"name\":\"DC.Description\",\"content\":\"In the aftermath of the 2016 United States presidential election, experts and journalists speculated that angry voters had supported the unexpected winner Donald Trump. The present study used a sample of 148 million tweets posted by U.S. citizens from across 1,347 counties, classified with regard to emotional content, to predict the election results at county level. As expected, Donald Trump received more support in counties where people tweeted more anger and negative emotions, even when various county characteristics and conservative vote choice in the preceding presidential election were controlled. These findings might be an outcome of emotional resonance—voters being attracted by political appeals that match their emotions—because Trump used more anger and negative emotion words in his campaign than the other presidential candidates in 2012 and 2016. The findings suggest that negative emotions played a critical role in the 2016 presidential election.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"name\":\"DC.Format\",\"content\":\"text/html\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"name\":\"DC.Relation.hasFormat\",\"content\":\"PDF\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"name\":\"DC.Relation.hasFormat\",\"content\":\"XML\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"name\":\"DC.Relation.hasVersion\",\"content\":\"313\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"name\":\"DC.Identifier\",\"content\":\"10.5334/irsp.256\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"name\":\"DC.Identifier.identifier\",\"content\":\"10.5334/irsp.256\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"DC.Date.issued\",\"content\":\"2019-01-10T14:45:42+00:00\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"name\":\"DC.Language\",\"content\":\"en\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"name\":\"DC.Language.language\",\"content\":\"en\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"name\":\"DC.Format.medium\",\"content\":\"text/html\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"22\",{\"name\":\"DC.Publisher.publisher\",\"content\":\"Ubiquity Press\"}],\"$Lfe\",\"$Lff\",\"$L100\",\"$L101\",\"$L102\",\"$L103\",\"$L104\",\"$L105\",\"$L106\",\"$L107\",\"$L108\",\"$L109\",\"$L10a\",\"$L10b\",\"$L10c\",\"$L10d\",\"$L10e\",\"$L10f\",\"$L110\",\"$L111\",\"$L112\",\"$L113\",\"$L114\",\"$L115\",\"$L116\",\"$L117\",\"$L118\",\"$L119\",\"$L11a\",\"$L11b\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"12f:I[27201,[\"https://journal-assets.ubiquity.press/2.27.0/_next/static/chunks/35j798tkrmk1i.js\"],\"IconMark\"]\nd2:[\"$\",\"span\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B28\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B28\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B28\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B28\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Grimm, Church, Katigbak, \u0026 Reyes, 1999\"}]}]}]\nd3:[\"$\",\"span\",\"29\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B47\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B47\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B47\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B47\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Na et al., 2010\"}]}]}]\nd4:[\"$\",\"span\",\"31\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B55\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B55\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B55\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B55\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Rentfrow, 2010\"}]}]}]\nd5:[\"$\",\"em\",\"33\",{\"children\":\"anger\"}]\nd6:[\"$\",\"span\",\"35\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B35\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B35\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B35\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B35\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Kitayama, Mesquita, \u0026 Karasawa, 2006\"}]}]}]\nd7:[\"$\",\"span\",\"37\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B34\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B34\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B34\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B34\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Kitayama, Conway III, Pietromonaco, Park, \u0026 Plaut, 2010\"}]}]}]\nd8:[\"$\",\"span\",\"39\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B65\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B65\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B65\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B65\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Suizzo et al., 2008\"}]}]}]\nd9:[\"$\",\"span\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B54\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B54\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B54\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B54\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"R Core Team, 2017\"}]}]}]\nda:[\"$\",\"span\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B36\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B36\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B36\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B36\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Kuhn et al., 2016\"}]}]}]\ndb:[\"$\",\"span\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B74\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B74\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B74\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B74\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Zou \u0026 Hastie, 2005\"}]}]}]\ndc:[\"$\",\"span\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B23\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B23\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B23\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B23\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Friedman, Hastie, \u0026 Tibshirani, 2010\"}]}]}]\ndd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"In a second set of analyses, we tested whether Trump’s campaign was exceptional in the expression of emotions that predicted his success on the county level. To this end, we compared mean values of emotional language indicators among the four presidential campaigns of 2012 and 2016. Because campaign data represent an (almost) complete inventory of tweets and campaign speeches rather than a sample, we did not apply inferential statistics. Instead, we calculated the mean differences between candidates’ campaigns with regard to the six Twitter language categories and regard them as the true mean difference of the population (of speeches and tweets). The mean effect size (Cohen’s \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"d\"}],\") for tweets and campaign speeches will be interpreted according to convention (\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B14\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B14\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B14\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B14\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Cohen, 1988\"}]}]}],\") and in terms of probability of superiority (\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"xref\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L54\",null,{\"scrollId\":\"B37\",\"linkProps\":{\"class\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#B37\",\"data-scroll\":\"#B37\",\"rel\":\"footnote\",\"id\":\"main-text-B37\",\"className\":\"scroll-link\"},\"children\":\"Lakens, 2013\"}]}]}],\").\"]}]\nde:[\"$\",\"div\",\"7\",{\"id\":\"T2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L7c\",null,{\"wrapperProps\":{\"className\":\"table-wrapper\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"caption\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"label\",\"children\":\"Table 2\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"children\":\"Linear Regression Model Predicting County-Level Results for Donald Trump in the U.S. Presidential Election 2016.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"table-scroll\",\"child